live-folder driver: rereads judged by every check, undelivered resume requests kept, teardown on every path (#52 Codex review)

- verifyControlPipe: a relay found gone is judged on its reread log by the
  same connectionFault() as the first read (unparsable, inputError, parent,
  relay start), so a relay that logs a fault (and its end) and exits between
  the first read and the liveness check fails the run instead of passing.
  The liveness check is injectable (running) so a test drives that exact
  interleaving.
- Resume requests whose forward failed (outputError.undelivered) stay in
  resumes and resumeRequests: the host asked. Each entry carries delivered
  (false for those). Oracle: scenario.json resumeObservation.fields.delivered
  (optional boolean), check.py refuses any other value, README documents it;
  an undelivered extra request still fails O3.resumeOnce.
- Adapter contract: cleanup({failed}), idempotent, leaves no process and
  keeps controlHost.observe. runLiveFolder tears down in a finally on every
  path: stop() if Record was asked and Stop was not, cleanup() once (bounded
  by CLEANUP_MS), stopRelays(), and the new stopLaunchers() kills control
  launchers still waiting in open() on a FIFO no relay opened. Each step is
  attempted, reported in out/teardown.json and never hides the run's own
  failure; a failed step fails a passing run.
- Tests (each fails on b0a066d): the reread race (unparsable, unparsable +
  end, inputError, inputError + end), undelivered requests kept and marked,
  runLiveFolder with a failure injected after Record (Stop, one cleanup, the
  relay stopped) and during the control launcher's startup (one cleanup, the
  launcher waiting on its FIFO killed), a missing or failing cleanup.

